\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come down, O Love Divine,
\par Seek Thou this soul of mine,
\par And visit it with Thine own ardour glowing ;
\par O Comforter, draw near,
\par Within my heatrt appear,
\par And kindle it, Thy holy flame bestowing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O let it freely burn,
\par Till earthly passions turn
\par To dust and ashes, in its heat consuming ;
\par And let Thy glorious light
\par Shine ever on my sight,
\par And clothe me round, the while my path illuming.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let holy charity
\par Mine outward vesture be,
\par And lowliness become mine inner clothing ;
\par True lowliness of heart,
\par Which takes the humbler part,
\par And o'er its own shortcomings weeps with loathing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And so the yearning strong,
\par With which the soul will long,
\par Shall far outpass the power of human telling ;
\par For none can guess its grace,
\par Till he become the place
\par Wherein the Holy Spirit makes His dwelling.
\par 
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

